ipd: RX buffers from a page_pool, one refill doorbell per poll, napi_alloc_skb

CPU 0 runs the only RX NAPI and sat at ~99% in ksoftirqd/0 under load
(2026-11-11).  Per received packet inno_ring_poll()/inno_rx_ring_poll()
did:

 * alloc_page() + dma_map_page(PAGE_SIZE) for the refill and
   dma_unmap_page(PAGE_SIZE) for the received buffer.  The PCIe host on
   this board is not marked dma-coherent in the device tree, so on arm64
   each map/unmap is a cache clean/invalidate over the whole 4 KiB page,
   for a ~1.5 KiB frame.
 * a wmb() + RXQ_x_DESC_PIDX MMIO write for every refilled descriptor.
 * alloc_skb() for the header skb.

Changes:

 * Each netdev RX ring gets a page_pool (PP_FLAG_DMA_MAP |
   PP_FLAG_DMA_SYNC_DEV).  Pages are mapped once and come back to the
   pool when the stack frees the skb (skb_mark_for_recycle), so the hot
   path has no page allocator and no map/unmap; the received bytes are
   made visible with a dma sync of wb.length instead of an unmap of the
   whole page.  inno_alloc_ring()/inno_free_ring()/refill_ring() use the
   pool for netdev rings; userspace rings are untouched.
 * The refill writes RXQ_x_DESC_PIDX once per ring per poll.
 * Descriptors of discarded packets keep their buffer and are simply
   posted again.  This replaces the need_release free and also stops the
   page leaks the old refill had for multi-descriptor discards and for a
   trailing descriptor holding only FCS bytes (it overwrote / dropped
   pages that were still allocated and mapped).
 * napi_alloc_skb() instead of alloc_skb(); napi_complete_done() instead
   of napi_complete().
 * The refill no longer returns -1 from the NAPI poll on a mapping error.

The page_pool allocation side is serialized by idev->napi_lock (RX poll,
refill, refill_ring() and the ring teardown).

Not verified on hardware when written.

